<BaseLayout title="Cookies policy | LearnNest" description="LearnNest cookies policy: the demo site uses no tracking cookies and no analytics that identify you." path="/cookies-policy">
  <h1>Cookies policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 22 November 2026. This policy is for the LearnNest demo site.</p>
  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small files a website can store in your browser to remember choices, such as your language or whether you are signed in.</p>
  <h2>What LearnNest uses</h2>
  <p><strong>None.</strong> This demo site sets no cookies, runs no tracking scripts, and uses no analytics that identify you. The tutor search and filters run in your browser only, and your choices are not sent anywhere.</p>
  <h2>Advertising cookies</h2>
  <p>There are no advertising cookies on LearnNest yet. If ads are added in future — for example, through Google AdSense — the advertising company may store cookies in your browser to show ads based on your visits to this and other websites. You can opt out of personalised advertising in <a href="https://ad.google.com/settings">Google Ads Settings</a> or at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices">www.aboutads.info/choices</a>.</p>
  <h2>If that changes</h2>
  <p>If cookies or analytics are added later — for example, to run a real service with accounts — this policy will be updated first, and a cookie notice will explain what is used and why.</p>
</BaseLayout>
